    "description": "This is Starship coming back from orbit, wrapped in plasma. 🔥\n\nOn Flight 14 (September 28, 2026), Starship reached orbit for the first time and carried real Starlink satellites. Coming home at about 27,000 km/h, the air in front of the ship is compressed and heated so much that it glows as plasma. Thousands of hexagonal heat shield tiles protect the steel ship, and SpaceX flew new tile upgrades on this flight. Starship then relit its engines, flipped upright and splashed down on target in the Pacific.\n\nNext time, they want to catch it with chopsticks. 👇\n\nSubscribe to Top Techs for more mind-blowing tech in under a minute.",
